menu "Screen cast (OTA-V3 continual file stream)"

config USING_SCREEN_CAST
    bool "Enable screen cast service"
    depends on FRAMED_PROTO && PKG_USING_LITTLEVGL2RTT
    default n
    help
        Receive a live screen / map cast pushed by the phone app over the BLE
        serial transmission channel (SiFli OTA-V3 "continual file" stream) and
        expose the decoded JPEG / audio / navigation frames to the application.

        Only the protocol component (FRAMED_PROTO) is needed: the frame layout,
        the response builders and the link are all shared. The firmware-update
        engine (OTA_EXT_V3) is not required.

config USING_SCREEN_CAST_WIFI
    bool "Enable WiFi (P2P GO + TCP) cast transport"
    depends on USING_SCREEN_CAST && RT_USING_WIFI && RT_USING_LWIP
    default n
    help
        Add a TCP transport on top of the screen cast service: the device
        starts a P2P GO hotspot and a TCP server, the phone joins the
        hotspot and connects to the server. The frame format is identical
        to the BT PAN transport used by solution2.0 (see src/wifi_tran).

        Requires a WiFi driver with P2P GO support (e.g. AIC8800D40L).

config USING_SCREEN_CAST_WIFI_AP
    bool "Use plain SoftAP instead of P2P GO"
    depends on USING_SCREEN_CAST_WIFI
    default n
    help
        Start a plain SoftAP (rt_wlan_start_ap) instead of a WiFi Direct
        P2P GO group (rt_wlan_p2p_go_start): the SSID shows up in the normal
        WiFi list, so any phone (including iPhone) can join it directly.
        The trade-off is that the phone drops its current WiFi while
        connected, and the channel is fixed to 6 (use rt_wlan_start_ap_adv()
        to pick a channel).

        Requires a driver with wlan_softap support (e.g. AIC8800D40L).

endmenu
